# A guest throws a rock at glass, and the host recalls the rock while it still shows it flying: a
# forced move to the host, then a placement at its spawn. What the guest sent of the flight before
# she heard (her states and her claim of the glass) reaches the host late and is dropped: the glass
# stands and the rock is home for everyone. She takes the rock again at once, and the host recalls
# it from her hand.
scenario recall_flight
scene glass_door
seed 3
guests 1
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2% reorder 10% reorder_delay 40ms

p1 grab rock_a as lift
at 1s p1 throw glass speed 7 as throw
# Measured: on the thrower's world the rock meets the glass 22 ticks after the throw, on tick 82.
# Each way takes at least 3 ticks (50 ms), so a recall from tick 80 to 84 reaches her after her
# contact, and her claim and release of it reach the host after the recall. On 84 the host's last
# taken state of the flight lies within the gate's 4 ticks of the contact, so the claim would fit a
# gate that kept the old number (test_body_sync_claims_mf_recall_keeps_number).
at 84t p0 recall rock_a as recall
# Her copy is home a one-way trip and a playback delay (at most 15 ticks) after the recall, within
# her reach; a lost record's resend fits too.
at 129t p1 grab rock_a as regrab
at 189t p0 recall rock_a as home

expect result lift granted
expect result throw done
expect result recall done
expect result regrab granted
expect result home done
# The late claim existed and the gate refused it as revoked: nothing came of it.
expect claims.count >= 1
expect claims_rejected.count >= 1
expect claim_effects.count <= 0
expect moved glass <= 1cm
# The late states existed and the host dropped them.
expect late_drops.count >= 1
# Home for everyone: the host put it at its spawn, and the guest agrees at rest.
expect moved rock_a <= 1cm
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
expect effects_once
# No ping-pong. Under interaction her only take is the flight's touch of the glass, refused: its
# agent, the rock, was the host's by then. The re-take is one grab, granted, and nothing of the
# host's touches her bodies.
expect takes.count <= 0
expect take_refusals.count <= 1
expect reclaims.count <= 0
